@startuml
!theme plain
title Cart · The four operations and their conflicts
autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Customer" as U
participant "Frontend" as F
participant "NestJS API" as A
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

note over A : Cart is exclusive to the customer role.\nManager and courier get 403 on all four

U -> F : Opens the cart
F -> A : GET /cart
A -> DB : Active cart
A --> F : 200 Cart
note right of A : An empty cart is empty items and a zero subtotal,\nnot a 404: the active cart always exists

== Add ==
U -> F : Adds a size
F -> A : POST /cart/items\nskuId + quantity
activate A
alt The SKU doesn't exist or its product is deactivated
  A --> F : 404 NotFound
else The quantity exceeds what's available
  A --> F : 409 Conflict
else The line would exceed 99
  A --> F : 409 Conflict
  note right of A : The two conflicts are told apart by the remedy:\nwaiting helps the first and never the second
else That SKU was already in the cart
  A -> DB : Adds to the existing line
  A --> F : 200 full Cart
  note right of DB : A second line for the same SKU is never created
else New line
  A -> DB : Creates the line
  A --> F : 201 full Cart
end
deactivate A

== Change and remove ==
F -> A : PATCH /cart/items/ID\nquantity
alt Exceeds what's available
  A --> F : 409 Conflict
else
  A --> F : 200 full Cart
end
F -> A : DELETE /cart/items/ID
A --> F : 200 full Cart

note over F, A #ffe0e0
  All three mutations return the **entire** cart, so the
  front never needs a second call to refresh the subtotal.
  The trade-off: cartItemId travels bare in the route. If the
  service doesn't check that the line belongs to the caller's
  cart, that's a textbook BOLA.
end note

note over A : The cart doesn't reserve stock.\nReserving is checkout's job

@enduml
